00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think one thing
that Donald Trump

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:02.869 size:84% position:42% line:92%
might be counting on is

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
the strength of the econom
right now.

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's certainly something
he talks about a lot.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.309
It came up a couple times in the
debate asking people on stage,

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.043 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"How do you respond to

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
the strong stock market,
low unemployment?"

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you actually think
the economy

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
could be a good talking poin
for Democrats.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean,
if you look at the polling

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:23.123
it is the one issue that he'
12 points up in approval on.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think there's a case to be
made for Democrats

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make the case
about why this economy

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
isn't actually working for
a lot of people.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you've got
a trillion-dollar tax cut.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
